# Documentation and progress

## Day one
Day one was where I gathered my referances and started laying everything out. I used notepad to get a feel of what the game would be like and the plot. I asked some people that I knew what would be a good start or if it was too simple. This project can't be too simple and I can't bite off more than I can chew, so it was very difficult to try and find a middle ground. I know thi project is going to be very repetitive and Ihave to add some elements to make the coding more complex.

# Trouble shooting
In day one, I already ran into an issue that VScode done that I did know of. It put all my folders into the same folder if nothing was in it, and not a subfolder. What had happened was, there was a box checked that grouped my folders. So once I unchecked it, it allowed my to add subfolders.

# A special thanks
    I would like to thank the people I reached out to that helped me build the plot and play tested the game. Even if it's just a small scene that didn't take long to play, it still ment a lot.